	<<addinlineevent "tie_stall_punishment_eavesdrop">>
		<<generate1>><<generate2>><<person1>>
		You try to listen to the farmhands' chatter.
		<br><br>
		<<silently>><<skulduggerydifficulty 1 1000>><</silently>>
		<<if $skulduggerysuccess>>
			<<if ($pain gte 60 and $stress gte ($stressmax / 5) * 3) and $rng lte 50>>
				But you're in too much pain to actually pay attention to what they say.
			<<elseif $necklaceThief is "player" and $rng lte 10>>
				You hear footsteps, coming from only one person. You feel something is different.
				<br><br>
				The steps get closer. They stop in front of your stall. A <<person>> stands before you. <<He>> almost gets paler and paler by the second.
				<br><br>
				You blink. A tall, pale figure has taken <<his>> place. It clutches its neck, a haunting rage in its eyes. Then, it speaks.
				<br><br>
				<span class="wraith">"Graverobber."</span>
				<br><br>
				You blink again. The pale figure is gone.<<stress 8>><<trauma 8>><<gstress>><<gtrauma>>
			<<else>>
				<<if Weather.precipitation isnot "none" and $rng gte 33>>
					"The weather's nice today," a <<person>> says as <<he>> changes the hay from a nearby stall. "I always found this type of climate relaxing to watch."
					<br>
					"Maybe if you don't have to work that day," the <<person2>><<person>> replies. "For example, today."
					<br>
					"You just hate everything I like."
					<br><br>
					The two of them wait for a little while before leaving the stalls.
				<</if>>
				<<rng>>
				<<if $rng gte 75>>
					"This stinks," a <<person>> complains. <<Hes>> carrying a fresh haybale while <<his>> partner, a <<person2>><<person>> removes the old hay, holding a bale of fresh hay.
					<br><br>
					The <<person>> doesn't reply, simply leaving when the job is done.
					<br><br>
					"Oi, where are you going?" the <<person1>><<person>> calls. Regardless, <<he>> follows behind.
				<<elseif $rng gte 50>>
					A <<person>> and a <<person2>><<person>> appear in the stalls. They pass right in front of you and stop in the next one. One of them is carrying a bundle of fresh hay, while the other one is carrying a basket full of shiny apples. Your stomach growls at the sight, and you can't help but wonder about how sweet and juicy they are. You wish you could eat at least one of them to satiate your curiosity.<<stress 4>><<gstress>>
					<br><br>
					"Sometimes I feel bad for the cattle and the steeds," the <<person>> says. "It must be difficult for them to watch us eat apples without having to earn them, at any moment we want." <<His>> tone makes you think <<hes>> saying it on purpose.
					<br><br>
					"I actually do feel bad for them, I think," replies the <<person1>><<person>> as <<he>> changes the hay. "But I'm not getting between Remy and <<nnpc_his "Remy">> ways."
					<br><br>
					The two of them leave the stalls before you can hear anything else.
				<<elseif $rng gte 25>>
					"Honestly, I haven't drank milk ever since I started working here," says the <<person>> changing hay in one of the nearby stalls. "I've grown a bit repulsed."
					<br><br>
					"I would drink the milk of one specific <<pcow>> here, if I'm being honest," replies another farmhand.
					<br><br>
					"I think I know which one you're referring to. <<pShe>> is really cute, I will admit it."
					<br><br>
					"Too sad <<pshe>> won't behave. I hope <<pshe>> doesn't make the same mistakes when <<pher>> punishment ends."
					<br><br>
					They leave the stalls.
				<<else>>
					"I've heard one of the farmhands tried to use the milking machine for their own milk. Not sure who," says the <<person>> changing hay in the stall in front of you.
					<br><br>
					"I've heard about it, too, and I'm not sure what to believe. Remy definitely wouldn't be happy to hear that, either way. <<nnpc_His "Remy">> machines are for <<nnpc_his "Remy">> animals only."
					<br><br>
					They leave the stalls.
				<</if>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			But you can't hear anything as they move on.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Livestock Tie Stall Punishment End]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

